Final research conclusion
The AICTE Security Deposit/FDR Management Portal is technically feasible using established web technologies, document AI and workflow automation. The strongest approach is to build a reliable management system first and introduce AI where it provides measurable value.

The proposed solution should be judged on three outcomes:
1. Accuracy: Financial instrument information is captured consistently, discrepancies are identified and verification evidence is preserved.
2. Timeliness: Maturity deadlines, renewals and pending release requests are visible and acted upon through reliable notifications and controlled workflows.
3. Accountability: Every important submission, correction, verification and approval can be traced to its source and responsible actor.
The most important unresolved dependencies are access to applicable regulatory rules, authorized verification mechanisms and representative test data. These should be addressed alongside development, not postponed until the end.

The immediate next milestone should be a working end-to-end prototype using synthetic FDR documents, deterministic validation, OCR-assisted extraction, maturity reminders, a renewal workflow, simulated verification and an auditable release-request process. Once that prototype has been evaluated, the team will have a sound basis for deciding which advanced AI features and external integrations are justified.